", "explanation": "Files changed: src/oscar/apps/catalogue/abstract_models.py (AbstractCategory.get_meta_title).

Root cause: the accessor returned `self.meta_title or ""`, so any category without an explicitly entered meta title rendered an empty SEO title. The sibling product accessor (AbstractProduct.get_meta_title) already falls back to `self.parent.meta_title` then the product title, and the category's own get_meta_description already falls back to the description; only the category meta title lacked a fallback. The template src/oscar/templates/oscar/catalogue/category.html calls `{{ category.get_meta_title }}` directly, so the empty string propagated straight into the page <title>.

Fix / fallback rule: `return self.meta_title or self.name` — an explicit meta title is used verbatim when present (no stored data changed, display unchanged for categories that do set one); otherwise the category name is used. No schema/migration changes; the accessor is a single read-only method with no other callers in the codebase besides the category template, so no other semantics are affected.

Unrelated observation (not included, to keep this patch focused): AbstractCategory.full_name joins ancestor names with `"".join(names)` instead of the class's `_full_name_separator` (" > "), which also looks like a regression worth a separate ticket."}}

